  "reason": "Current evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool and scvi is the strongest setting (accuracy 0.650, F1 0.628), and multiprofile avgpool has also helped PCA-based RNA models. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the untested scGPT representation can improve on scvi under the same strong profile and aggregation setting. config_008 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi to scGPT while holding multiprofile and avgpool fixed, so it isolates the effect of representation. This is the best next experiment because it can either establish a new best RNA baseline or prune many scGPT-based configurations before spending budget on more complex multimodal fusion."
